IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa-employee`
IMPORT `fwa-day-one`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- THE EMPLOYER'S SEAT LAYER, for day one.
--
-- SEAT: the employer -- a small business owner or a company taking on employees (Daniel's Jarrah Legal Technologies
-- with its first three, d044). "What must I give a new employee, or a new casual, on day one? Can the contract give
-- them less than the NES? What records must I keep, and for how long?"
--
-- This is the SECOND seat on this encoding, beside the employee's (fwa-employee.l4 and fwa-day-one.l4), under the
-- ruling of 21 October 2026 on more than one seat. Nothing here is new law: every question calls a rule in
-- fwa-day-one.l4 or fwa-employee.l4 and restates none, so the two seats cannot disagree; the mirror cases in
-- fwa-cases-employer.l4 show it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the employer can state, each with an @desc worded
-- from the employer's seat ("How many employees do you have ...?").
--
-- NAMES. Every name defined here begins "As the employer, " so that none can clash with the employee's questions.
--
-- Questions an employer would ask that the modules do not decide (the award that covers the employees, the minimum
-- wage, the s 15A casual test, whether a term is an agreement an NES provision allows) are taken as facts or left out;
-- see NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- day one: the employer's questions`

§§ `ss 44, 60, 61 -- the National Employment Standards as a floor`

@export As the employer, can the employment contract give this employee less than the National Employment Standards (ss 44, 60, 61)?
GIVEN `the person is a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your national system employee (you are a national system employer, such as a company, and they are not on an unpaid vocational placement)
      `what the term does` IS A `What the contract term does` @desc What the contract term (for example a probation clause) does compared with the National Employment Standards
GIVETH A `Where the contract term stands`
DECIDE `As the employer, can the contract give less than the NES` IS
    `the NES against a contract term` `the person is a national system employee` `what the term does`

@export As the employer, would I contravene the National Employment Standards (s 44)?
GIVEN `the person is a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your national system employee
      `I have not given something an NES provision requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to give the employee something a National Employment Standard requires (leave, notice, a statement, and so on)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I contravened the NES` IF
    `the employer has contravened s 44` `the person is a national system employee` `I have not given something an NES provision requires`

§§ `ss 125, 125B, 333K -- the information statements`

@export As the employer, which information statements must I give this new employee, before or as soon as practicable after they start (ss 125, 125B(1)(a), 333K)?
GIVEN `the person is a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your national system employee
      `they start as a casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they start as a casual employee: no firm advance commitment to continuing and indefinite work, and a casual loading or casual rate (s 15A)
      `the contract ends at the end of a set period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract says it ends at the end of an identifiable period (a date, a task or a season), even if it can also end earlier
      `I gave them the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have employed them before: whether you gave them the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this start
      `I gave them the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have employed them before as a casual: whether you gave them the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before this start
GIVETH A `Day-one answer`
DECIDE `As the employer, which statements must I give on day one` IS
    `the day-one statements`
        `the person is a national system employee` `they start as a casual` `the contract ends at the end of a set period`
        `I gave them the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this start`
        `I gave them the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before this start`

@export As the employer, must I give this employee the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)?
GIVEN `the person is a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your national system employee
      `I gave them the statement in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have employed them before: whether you gave them the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this start
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, must I give the Fair Work Information Statement` IF
    `the employer must give the Fair Work Information Statement` `the person is a national system employee` `I gave them the statement in the 12 months before this start`

@export As the employer, must I give this casual the Casual Employment Information Statement at this point (s 125B)?
GIVEN `the person is a casual employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your casual employee (s 15A)
      `the person is a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your national system employee
      `the point reached` IS A `Casual statement occasion` @desc Which point the casual has reached in their employment with you
      `how many employees I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees you have at that point, counting the casual and other casuals only if they are employed regularly and systematically, and counting employees of associated entities (s 23)
      `I gave them the statement in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have employed them before as a casual: whether you gave them this statement in the 12 months before this start
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, must I give the Casual Employment Information Statement` IF
    `the employer must give the Casual Employment Information Statement`
        `the person is a casual employee` `the person is a national system employee` `the point reached`
        `how many employees I have` `I gave them the statement in the 12 months before this start`

§§ `s 535, regs 3.31-3.42 -- the records I must keep`

@export As the employer, what employee records must I make and keep for this employee (s 535, regs 3.32-3.40)?
GIVEN `they are casual or irregular part-time, paid by time worked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual or irregular part-time employee guaranteed a rate of pay by reference to time worked
      `they are entitled to a bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive payment or allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is entitled to any bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive-based payment or other allowance
      `a penalty rate or loading is payable for their overtime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you must pay a penalty rate or loading for overtime hours the employee actually works
      `we agreed in writing to average their hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the employee have agreed in writing to average their hours of work
      `they are entitled to leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is entitled to any leave (paid or unpaid)
      `we agreed to cash out leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the employee have agreed to cash out some accrued leave
      `I must make super contributions for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are required to make superannuation contributions for the employee
      `we have an individual flexibility arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the employee have agreed an individual flexibility arrangement in writing
      `I gave them a guarantee of annual earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the employee a guarantee of annual earnings (s 330)
      `their employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee's employment with you has ended
GIVETH A LIST OF `Employee record`
DECIDE `As the employer, what records must I keep` IS
    `the records required`
        `they are casual or irregular part-time, paid by time worked`
        `they are entitled to a bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive payment or allowance`
        `a penalty rate or loading is payable for their overtime`
        `we agreed in writing to average their hours`
        `they are entitled to leave`
        `we agreed to cash out leave`
        `I must make super contributions for them`
        `we have an individual flexibility arrangement`
        `I gave them a guarantee of annual earnings`
        `their employment has ended`

@export As the employer, for how many years must I keep each employee record (s 535(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how many years must I keep records` IS `the years records must be kept`

@export As the employer, may I stop keeping an employee record I made this many years ago (s 535(1))?
GIVEN `years since I made the record` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years ago you made the record
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, may I stop keeping this record` IF
    `the record may be discarded` `years since I made the record`

@export As the employer, is this employee record kept in the form the Regulations require (reg 3.31(1))?
GIVEN `it is legible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the record is legible
      `it is in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the record is in the English language
      `an inspector could readily get at it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the record is in a form readily accessible to a Fair Work inspector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, is my record in the required form` IF
    `the record is in the prescribed form` `it is legible` `it is in English` `an inspector could readily get at it`

@export As the employer, how quickly must I let an employee or former employee inspect and copy their record once they ask (reg 3.42)?
GIVEN `I keep the records where they work or worked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you keep the records at the premises where the employee works (or worked)
GIVETH A `Time to produce a record`
DECIDE `As the employer, how quickly must I produce a record` IS
    `the time to produce a record` `I keep the records where they work or worked`

§§ `s 536 -- pay slips, from the first pay`

-- s 536(1), in fwa-employee.l4: a pay slip "within one working day of paying an amount to the employee".
@export As the employer, is the pay slip I gave in time (s 536(1))?
GIVEN `working days after I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days after paying the employee you gave the pay slip
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, was my pay slip in time` IF
    `Was my pay slip in time` `working days after I paid`

§§ `s 557C -- if I kept no records (only if an employee claims against you)`

@export As the employer, if I did not keep the record, must I disprove what the employee alleges (s 557C)?
GIVEN `the claim is about the NES, an award, an agreement, the minimum wage, or how I paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee claims you contravened the NES, a modern award, an enterprise agreement, a workplace determination, a national minimum wage or equal remuneration order, the rules on how and how often you pay, or the ban on unreasonable requirements to spend or pay money
      `I had to keep a record or give a pay slip about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law required you to make and keep a record, let the employee inspect one, or give a pay slip, about the matter alleged
      `I did not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to do so
      `if the court accepts my reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court accepts your reasonable excuse for the failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, must I disprove the allegation` IF
    `the employer must disprove the allegation`
        `the claim is about the NES, an award, an agreement, the minimum wage, or how I paid`
        `I had to keep a record or give a pay slip about it`
        `I did not`
        `if the court accepts my reasonable excuse`
